"""Shared Work validation guidance; enforcement remains in workflow controllers."""
POLICY = "RISK-BASED VALIDATION\nBefore editing, classify the current requested change LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH by behavior, blast radius and reversibility, not file extension alone. Record risk, reasons, affected apps/journeys, baseline commit, focused commands, escalation triggers and remaining gaps in implementation-plan.md (or the existing validation section). State this briefly to the user. Reassess if scope expands. Use the highest material risk in a mixed change. Follow mandatory repository/CI checks and explicit user requirements.\n\nLOW: isolated CSS/markup/template/presentation changes with no business logic, identity, persistence, security or shared contract changes. Frontend TS/Svelte is LOW only under those conditions. A migration scaffold or inactive flag is LOW only if it changes no executable behavior or data. Storage additions/changes are LOW only for isolated, non-sensitive, reversible content with no existing-data or access impact.\nRun focused component tests and the affected browser journey; check narrow phone layout, relevant modes/tenants, keyboard/focus/accessibility and the actual visible result. Use a relevant typecheck when types or templates change. For a pure document change, validate links/content rather than launching an application suite. No automatic Claude review for an ordinary LOW task unless explicitly requested or required by repository policy. Report focused validation, not whole-feature certification.\n\nMEDIUM: bounded SvelteKit/backend/PHP service behavior, additive data changes with compatible defaults, shared UI behavior or state, and changes with a known, contained integration boundary. Run LOW checks as applicable, affected unit/integration suites and direct consumers, success and failure/validation cases, permission boundaries where touched, persistence/reload and backwards compatibility where relevant. Exercise the affected end-to-end journey; include Chromium/WebKit when browser behavior differs or the feature targets iOS. Run affected package typechecks/lint/build as appropriate. Require independent review before claiming ready to merge.\n\nHIGH: data deletion/transformation, identity/schema migrations, authentication/authorization/privacy/payments, destructive storage operations, broad shared contracts, executable feature flags controlling sensitive behavior, Docker/runtime/build/deployment changes, dependencies/lockfiles and CI/hooks/config changes affecting execution or safety. Cosmetic metadata-only edits may be lower risk with an explicit reason. Run comprehensive regression for all affected systems and direct dependents, integration and critical cross-app journeys, relevant supported browsers, builds/static checks, security/negative cases and migration/backfill/idempotence/rollback tests on disposable data as applicable. Use the full repository suite for cross-cutting impact, uncertain blast radius or a release checkpoint; omit unrelated platforms only with recorded justification. Require independent review and explicit human acceptance of material risks before release. Never operate on production data to validate a migration. A review is not permission to merge, push or deploy; HIGH is not automatic permission to close or abandon a PR.\n\nTEST DISCIPLINE\nUse existing project runners and CI commands. For a bug fix, prove a relevant regression test fails before the fix and passes after where feasible; otherwise record the evidence gap. Never weaken assertions, hide skipped tests, replace real behavior with mocks or report unavailable/manual checks as passed. Stop after the selected checks pass: broaden or repeat only for subsequent relevant edits, failures, uncertain impact, explicit instructions or a release checkpoint, and explain why. Reuse recorded evidence only for unchanged relevant source/config/environment. Long runs need a progress update explaining what remains. If runner limits cannot accommodate required checks, report the gap and use the project's existing CI/approved test path; do not silently reduce coverage or raise limits.\n\nSCOPE AND REVIEW\nKeep current-change validation distinct from earlier stream-wide work. Do not automatically rerun every historical acceptance item for a small visual tweak, and do not erase or reclassify earlier blockers. Full-feature readiness still requires all its acceptance criteria. Scope an independent review explicitly to the agreed change and affected regressions; changing existing review scope requires agreement and must retain outstanding broader gaps. Native/device checks remain open until actually performed.\nAn explicit Implement through review or work review request still runs independent review even for LOW risk. The controller owns that review; agents in that flow must not launch it themselves. Normal MEDIUM/HIGH Work tasks use the bounded final review after routine checks pass. Claude remains Sonnet/medium, at most 24 turns/20 minutes per call, one initial plus one follow-up; no automatic new cycle, extra Claude helpers or paid API fallback. Do not consume a review merely to rediscover known missing evidence; report that blocker first. A completed review may correctly require changes or remain incomplete. Only the controller's verified verdict is independent approval for its exact recorded version and scope.\n"

POLICY += """
LOCAL COMPLETION GATE
Before selected checks run, create/fill docs/handoffs/<stream>/validation-plan.json (work complete <stream> --init creates a non-passing template). Fields: version 1; risk low/medium/high; scope, rationale and coverage explaining this change, affected behavior and why selected tests suffice; checks listing existing tests-input/review-input check IDs; limitations listing any concrete gaps. High risk also needs risk_controls covering regression scope and recovery/rollback. Keep it brief for a title/style change. Use the project's existing tests, not a new framework. Evidence must match the current checkout; write assessment and test inputs before testing.
For ordinary Work completion, use work tests run <stream> for selected finite checks, then work complete <stream>. Reuse a current passing recorded run instead of rerunning. work complete only checks evidence; it never starts tests or Claude. A low-risk focused pass needs no automatic review. Medium/high risk needs current independent review, or a concrete review_deferred_reason (at least 20 characters) to report completed-with-limitations, never verified/merge-ready. Existing unresolved review findings cannot be bypassed this way. Missing, failed, stale or modified logs never count as passed. Report blockers; do not expand scope, retry indefinitely, weaken tests or reset Claude counters just to obtain a receipt.
Within Implement through review, use the existing work flow ready receipt instead: it checks the risk assessment; the controller then executes the declared checks and review and checks completion before accepting verified. Do not launch work tests or work complete inside that active workflow. Preserve its initial-plus-follow-up Claude limits. Completing a small scoped change does not certify previous unverified work. No completion receipt authorizes merge, push or deploy. This is a local workflow safeguard, not future CI/CD enforcement.
"""
